{0 Supported libraries}

Learn which OCaml libraries and standard library features run in a Worker. The
list is not complete. A library works when it compiles with wasm_of_ocaml and
needs no operating system feature that a Worker does not have, such as threads
or sockets. A new dependency increases the size of your Worker. See
{{!page-testing}Testing and limits}.

{1 Checked in workerd}

The route list of [examples/features] runs each of these in a deployed Worker:

- Effects: OCaml 5 effect handlers, with and without awaiting Promises.
- [Hashtbl], [Lazy], [Seq], [Printexc] and [Random.State].
- [Int32], [Int64], [Float] and [Bigarray].
- [Marshal].
- [Str] regular expressions.
- [Digest]: MD5 and BLAKE2b.
- {!Workero.Timer}, {!Workero.Date}, {!Workero.Crypto} and {!Workero.Console}.
- JavaScript interop with [Js_of_ocaml], for example [JSON].

{1 [jsonkit]}

{{:https://github.com/melange-community/jsonkit}jsonkit} reads and writes JSON,
with a ppx that derives the functions. {!Workero.JSON} builds on it and gives
values as [Jsonkit.t]. It does not re-export jsonkit. opam installs jsonkit with
workero. Add [jsonkit] to the [libraries] of your [dune] file to use it. See
{{!page-requests}Requests and responses}.

{1 Server-side React}

[examples/react] renders a page from [.mlx] components with a trimmed copy of
server-reason-react. It uses the synchronous render path only.

{1 Embedded files}

A Worker has no file system. To read a file at run time, embed it with the
wasm_of_ocaml [--file] flag. The program reads it with [open_in]:

{@dune[
(executable
 (name main)
 (modes wasm)
 (libraries workero)
 (link_deps motd.txt)
 (wasm_of_ocaml
  (flags
   (--file motd.txt:/static/motd.txt))))
]}

{1 Libraries that need native code}

A library with C stubs that have no wasm implementation fails the build.
[workero build] lists the missing functions. Provide a wasm implementation with
[(wasm_of_ocaml (wasm_files ...))], or drop the library. See {{!page-cli}the
CLI}.
